C++ error handling: luaD_throw throws a lua_exception; LUAI_TRY catches lua_exception& and turns a
std::exception const& into a Lua error with luaG_runerror(L, "%s", e.what()).

Justification (PLAYER bytes): RTTI .?AVlua_exception@@ at 0x00d94b14. luaD_throw 0x008ab530 builds
{vftable 0x00b85540, L, errorJmp, committed=0} on top of std::exception::exception() and calls
_CxxThrowException. luaD_rawrunprotected 0x008aadd0: its FuncInfo 0x00cc4ec8 has try 0 with catch
(lua_exception&) at 0x008aae15 and catch (std::exception const&, adjectives 9) at 0x008aae30, which
calls e.what() and luaG_runerror(L, "%s" 0x00be1f20, ...) inside an inner try whose catch
(lua_exception&) is 0x008aae59; each catch sets byte [e+0x14] (committed) = 1 and status = -1 if 0.
The class members match: what() 0x008aad30 = lua_tostring(L,-1); ~lua_exception 0x008aad50 resets
errorJmp->status and pops one value unless committed; copy ctor 0x008ab5b0 commits the source.
(2016 catches RBX::base_exception instead of std::exception; no RBX::base_exception RTTI exists in
PLAYER.)

